text":"If you dig a pit and throw your trash in, you have a landfill."},{"role":"problem","text":"But dirty trash juice leaks straight down into the groundwater you drink."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you lay a thick clay base, but it is still not enough."},{"role":"fix2","text":"You add a thick black plastic sheet."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a landfill liner."},{"role":"how","text":"A pipe drains the collected juice into a tank beside the pit."},{"role":"fact","text":"Sealed this tight, trash barely rots at all once it is buried."},{"role":"factProof","text":"A 1952 newspaper dug up decades later was still readable word for word."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But trapped trash still makes gas, so a pipe carries it out."},{"role":"myth","text":"That flame is not waste burning, it is gas making electricity nearby."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a grass cap, a fence, and a few young trees."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a landfill."}]}